      "summaries": {
        "en": "cc-switch is a cross-platform desktop tool that solves the fragmentation problem when working with multiple AI coding assistants like Claude Code and Codex by providing a unified interface. Its technical strength lies in being built with Rust, which ensures high performance and reliability for managing different AI providers through a single application. Developers can use it to streamline their workflow by switching between AI coding tools without changing environments, making it practical for experimenting with different models' coding suggestions directly in their development setup.",
        "zh": "cc-switch是一款跨平台桌面工具，解决了开发者同时使用Claude Code、Codex等多种AI编程助手时界面分散的痛点，通过统一平台整合不同服务。其技术亮点在于采用Rust语言开发，确保了高性能和稳定性，能够可靠地管理多个AI提供商的接口。用户可以通过它在一个应用中无缝切换不同AI编程工具，无需反复配置环境，非常适合在实际开发中快速对比和测试各模型的代码生成能力，提升编程效率。",
        "es": "cc-switch is a cross-platform desktop tool that solves the fragmentation problem when working with multiple AI coding assistants like Claude Code and Codex by providing a unified interface. Its technical strength lies in being built with Rust, which ensures high performance and reliability for managing different AI providers through a single application. Developers can use it to streamline their workflow by switching between AI coding tools without changing environments, making it practical for experimenting with different models' coding suggestions directly in their development setup.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "cc-switch stands out for ai-tools, claude-code, and codex in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "cc-switch is a cross-platform desktop tool that solves the fragmentation problem when working with multiple AI coding assistants like Claude Code and Codex by providing a unified interface. Its technical strength lies in being built with Rust, which ensures high performance and reliability for managing different AI providers through a single application. Developers can use it to streamline their workflow by switching between AI coding tools without changing environments, making it practical for experimenting with different models' coding suggestions directly in their development setup.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
